<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manghit dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1756–1920</span> · Also known as Manghits</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Manghits were an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> tribe whose chiefs ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> from the mid-18th century until 1920. Muhammad Rahim, who held the office of atalik, took effective power under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s protection, and in 1785 his relative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-murad">Shah Murad</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Bukhara, the dynasty taking the title emir. The last emir, Alim Khan, fled when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> took Bukhara in 1920.</p></div>
